Writes /home/lumen/minerva/context/SESSION-BRIEFING.md: a generated situational
briefing written FOR the incoming agent, not an archive. claude_context.sh --core
prints it right after the live VERIFY block, before HANDOFF.md and before the
claude_memory.md selector output.

NOT the same file as /home/lumen/scratch/subtraction/SESSION-BRIEFING.md (the
hand-appended, append-only session log). This one is regenerated whole on every
run and never hand-edited. It lives in minerva/context/ (gitignored, next to
LIVE_FLEET_STATE.md) so a generated file never dirties the minerva primary tree.

Sections (all generated, no hand prose):
  0 HEALTH LINE      wq#5082: dispatch latch, dispatch/sweep timer state, usage freshness,
                     fworkers running. Red marks when the pipeline is off.
  1 RECENT CHATS     claude.ai chat-list snapshot (context/recent_chats.json, written
                     by `session-briefing ingest-chats` from a browser session's
                     recent_chats output) merged with CCC-exported conversations in
                     /home/lumen/publish/inbox. When that is thin or stale, a labelled
                     PROXY list from claude-session episodes is shown as well.
  2 ACTIVE WORK      wq claimed / frank_gated / pending_review / blocked + pending grants
  2a PROMPT PIPELINE wq#5082: every paste prompt in fleet-intel/prompts with its ticket status,
                     grouped READY / RUNNING / DONE-not-archived / OTHER / UNTICKETED
  2b NEXT UP         wq#5082: top 5 unblocked, non-gated open tickets by effective priority,
                     with the router's model tuple (stamp if present, else router --dry-run)
  3 LAST 48H         episodes (what changed, what failed), Frank-stated facts, decisions
  4 STANDING ORDERS  parsed from claude_memory.md (hand prose first, then decisions)
  5 OPEN HANDOFFS    open tickets whose notes say handoff / incomplete / not done

Hard cap 400 lines. Over the cap it trims, in order: oldest episodes, lowest-pri
blocked tickets, lowest-pri frank_gated tickets, standing orders, handoffs, chats.

Usage:
  session-briefing                          render to the default path
  session-briefing --out PATH               render elsewhere (tests)
  session-briefing --stdout                 print, write nothing
